 "I would try them all and pick the one with the lowest error.",
 "Exponential smoothing is a quick, robust baseline for each series and needs little tuning. Prophet adds trend changes, seasonality and holidays with readable components, but it is not always the most accurate. Gradient boosting trains one global model across all 200 products using lag features, calendar features, price and promotions, so it can learn from related products and handle short histories. I'd compare all three with walk-forward validation on the metric the business cares about, ship the simple baseline first, and move to the global model if it wins by a margin that justifies the extra pipeline.",
